From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:10:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dashboard): drop the default model with its removed
 provider

Removing an API key or a sign-in left model.provider and model.default naming a provider with no credential, so every new chat failed on authentication; removing a custom endpoint dropped its provider but kept model.default. dashboard.detach_removed_default (false = off) drops the main model together with its provider, so session.create refuses plainly as no_model_configured until another model is chosen. A provider that still holds a key elsewhere (another of its variables, or the environment) keeps its default.
---
 hermes_cli/config_defaults.py                 |  4 +
 hermes_cli/web_routers/config_env.py          | 64 +++++++++++-
 hermes_cli/web_routers/oauth.py               |  9 ++
 .../hermes_cli/test_detach_removed_default.py | 98 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 172 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/hermes_cli/test_detach_removed_default.py

